[size=5][b]PiP Player - picture-in-picture videos in Skyrim[/b][/size]

[size=4][b]About[/b][/size]

PiP Player plays a video in a corner of the screen while you keep playing Skyrim or Enderal. Paste a YouTube link, a direct video link, a livestream, or a file on your PC; it plays at the size, corner, and opacity you choose, and picks up where you left it next time.

It is drawn inside the game's own frame, so it works in exclusive fullscreen and borderless window, on Windows and under CrossOver on macOS.

[size=4][b]Features[/b][/size]

[list]
[*]YouTube videos and live streams, local video files, direct links ([font=Courier New].mp4[/font], [font=Courier New].webm[/font], ...), and HLS streams
[*]Control panel that pauses the game: paste a link, play the clipboard, recent videos with Resume, pause, stop, volume, quality, and layout settings applied live
[*]On-video controls: title, play/pause, 5 second skips, seek bar; click the video to pause, drag it to another corner
[*]Switch YouTube quality while playing (360p to 4K, 720p by default)
[*]Remembers the last 100 videos and where you left them; resumes your last video when you load a save
[*]Quick keys for pause and show/hide; all keys remappable
[*]No ESP, no scripts, nothing stored in saves: add or remove it at any time
[/list]

[size=4][b]Requirements[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][url=https://skse.silverlock.org/]SKSE64[/url] for your game version
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/32444]Address Library for SKSE Plugins[/url] (Enderal SE already includes it)
[*]Skyrim Special Edition / Anniversary Edition 1.5.97, 1.6.x, or 1.7.x, or Enderal SE
[*]For YouTube: yt-dlp and QuickJS (included in the "with YouTube" download, or see below)
[/list]

[size=4][b]Installation[/b][/size]

Install with Mod Organizer 2 or Vortex, or extract the archive into your game's [font=Courier New]Data[/font] folder. There is no plugin to enable in the load order.

[size=3][b]Downloads[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]PiPPlayer with YouTube[/b] - plugin, video player (libmpv), yt-dlp, QuickJS - everything
[*][b]PiPPlayer[/b] - plugin, video player (libmpv) - local files, direct links, streams (no YouTube)
[*][b]PiPPlayer YouTube Tools[/b] - yt-dlp, QuickJS - adds YouTube to the plain PiPPlayer download
[/list]

All three are on the [url=https://github.com/anuvgupta/skypip/releases/latest]GitHub releases page[/url].

[size=3][b]Getting YouTube support[/b][/size]

If you installed the plain [b]PiPPlayer[/b] file, pick one:

[list=1]
[*][b]Add the YouTube Tools download.[/b] Get [font=Courier New]PiPPlayer-YouTube-Tools-<version>.zip[/font] from [url=https://github.com/anuvgupta/skypip/releases/latest]GitHub releases[/url] and install it like any mod (or extract it into [font=Courier New]Data[/font]).
[*][b]Get the two tools yourself.[/b]
[list]
[*][font=Courier New]yt-dlp.exe[/font] from [url=https://github.com/yt-dlp/yt-dlp/releases/latest]yt-dlp releases[/url] (tested: 2026.08.19)
[*][font=Courier New]qjs-windows-x86_64.exe[/font] from [url=https://github.com/quickjs-ng/quickjs/releases/latest]QuickJS-NG releases[/url] (tested: v0.17.0); rename it to [font=Courier New]qjs.exe[/font]
[*]Put both in [font=Courier New]Data/SKSE/Plugins/PiPPlayer/[/font], next to [font=Courier New]libmpv-2.dll[/font]. With MO2, put them in that folder inside the PiPPlayer mod (right-click the mod → Open in Explorer).
[/list]
[*][b]Use the all-in-one download.[/b] Replace PiPPlayer with [font=Courier New]PiPPlayer-<version>-with-YouTube.zip[/font] from [url=https://github.com/anuvgupta/skypip/releases/latest]GitHub releases[/url].
[/list]

Without the tools, YouTube links show a message pointing here; everything else plays normally.

[size=3][b]Files[/b][/size]

[code]Data/SKSE/Plugins/PiPPlayer.dll
Data/SKSE/Plugins/PiPPlayer.ini
Data/SKSE/Plugins/PiPPlayer/libmpv-2.dll
Data/SKSE/Plugins/PiPPlayer/yt-dlp.exe      (YouTube)
Data/SKSE/Plugins/PiPPlayer/qjs.exe         (YouTube)[/code]

[size=4][b]How to use[/b][/size]

[list=1]
[*]Load a save and press [b]Left Bracket[/b] to open the control panel. The game pauses and a mouse cursor appears.
[*]Paste a link (Ctrl+V) into the box and press [b]Play[/b], or copy a link first and press [b]Play clipboard[/b], or pick a video from [b]Recent[/b] and press [b]Resume[/b].
[*]Press [b]Left Bracket[/b], Esc, or the panel's X to close it. The video keeps playing in its corner while you play.
[/list]

While the panel is open, the video shows its title, a play/pause button, 5 second skip buttons, and a seek bar. Click the video to pause it, or drag it to move it to another corner.

[size=3][b]Controls[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Left Bracket[/b] - Open or close the control panel
[*][b]Right Bracket[/b] - Pause or resume
[*][b]Backslash[/b] - Show or hide the player
[*][b]Esc[/b] - Close the control panel
[/list]

These are the three keys right of P on a US keyboard; on other layouts the same physical keys are used. On a Mac under CrossOver, Cmd+V also pastes in the panel when CrossOver passes Cmd through.

[size=4][b]Configuration[/b][/size]

Most settings are in the control panel and are saved automatically. Everything else is in [font=Courier New]Data/SKSE/Plugins/PiPPlayer.ini[/font] (edit it while the game is closed).

[list]
[*][b][font=Courier New]Overlay / Corner[/font][/b] - [font=Courier New]BottomLeft[/font] - [font=Courier New]TopLeft[/font], [font=Courier New]TopRight[/font], [font=Courier New]BottomLeft[/font], [font=Courier New]BottomRight[/font]
[*][b][font=Courier New]Width[/font][/b] - [font=Courier New]480[/font] - video width in pixels at the game's resolution
[*][b][font=Courier New]MarginX[/font], [font=Courier New]MarginY[/font][/b] - [font=Courier New]24[/font] - distance from the screen edges
[*][b][font=Courier New]Opacity[/font][/b] - [font=Courier New]1.0[/font] - [font=Courier New]0.05[/font] to [font=Courier New]1.0[/font]
[*][b][font=Courier New]CornerRadius[/font][/b] - [font=Courier New]6[/font] - [font=Courier New]0[/font] for square corners
[*][b][font=Courier New]Playback / Volume[/font][/b] - [font=Courier New]50[/font] - [font=Courier New]0[/font] to [font=Courier New]100[/font]
[*][b][font=Courier New]Loop[/font][/b] - [font=Courier New]false[/font] - repeat the video
[*][b][font=Courier New]Url[/font][/b] - empty - starting text of the panel's link box
[*][b][font=Courier New]YouTubeMaxHeight[/font][/b] - [font=Courier New]720[/font] - highest YouTube quality ([font=Courier New]0[/font] = best); lower uses less CPU
[*][b][font=Courier New]ResumeOnStart[/font][/b] - [font=Courier New]true[/font] - play the last video when a save loads
[*][b][font=Courier New]Hotkeys / TogglePanel[/font], [font=Courier New]TogglePause[/font], [font=Courier New]ToggleVisible[/font][/b] - [b]Left Bracket[/b], [b]Right Bracket[/b], [b]Backslash[/b] - key names ([font=Courier New]F8[/font], [font=Courier New]Home[/font], [font=Courier New]K[/font], [font=Courier New]Numpad5[/font], ...) or DirectInput codes
[/list]

The game log [font=Courier New]Documents/My Games/Skyrim Special Edition/SKSE/PiPPlayer.log[/font] warns if one of your keys is also bound to a game control.

[size=4][b]YouTube notes[/b][/size]

[list]
[*]A YouTube link takes a few seconds to start while yt-dlp looks it up.
[*]Private, age-restricted, and members-only videos do not play (there is no sign-in).
[*]YouTube changes often break older yt-dlp versions. If YouTube links stop working, press [b]Update yt-dlp[/b] in the control panel.
[*]yt-dlp streams the video for personal viewing; downloading from YouTube is against YouTube's terms of service.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Resume[/b][/size]

Every video picks up where you left it. The last 100 videos and their positions are kept in [font=Courier New]Documents/My Games/Skyrim Special Edition/SKSE/PiPPlayer_History.txt[/font]. Positions in the first 10 seconds or the last 15 seconds start the video over.

[size=4][b]Compatibility[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Game versions:[/b] Skyrim SE/AE 1.5.97, 1.6.x, 1.7.x; tested on Enderal SE (1.7.104). Not for Skyrim VR or LE.
[*][b]Enderal SE:[/b] supported; Enderal already includes Address Library.
[*][b]macOS (CrossOver):[/b] supported and tested. Video decodes on the CPU there; lower [font=Courier New]YouTubeMaxHeight[/font] if the game slows down.
[*][b]SSE Display Tweaks:[/b] compatible.
[*][b]ENB, ReShade, Community Shaders:[/b] not tested yet; reports welcome.
[*]Load order: none (no ESP).
[/list]

[size=4][b]Known limitations[/b][/size]

[list]
[*]Video controls appear while the control panel is open, not over game menus.
[*]No gamepad support yet.
[*]An audio-only file shows "Buffering..." because it has no picture.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Troubleshooting[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Nothing happens when I press [b]Left Bracket[/b]:[/b] check [font=Courier New]Documents/My Games/Skyrim Special Edition/SKSE/skse64.log[/font] for [font=Courier New]PiPPlayer.dll ... loaded correctly[/font]. If it is missing, check SKSE and Address Library.
[*][b]A key does something in the game too:[/b] see [font=Courier New]PiPPlayer.log[/font] for conflicts and pick another key in the INI.
[*][b]YouTube says it needs the YouTube tools:[/b] see "Getting YouTube support" above.
[*][b]YouTube stopped working:[/b] press [b]Update yt-dlp[/b] in the control panel.
[*]Anything else: attach [font=Courier New]PiPPlayer.log[/font] when you report it.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Uninstall[/b][/size]

Remove the mod in your mod manager, or delete [font=Courier New]PiPPlayer.dll[/font], [font=Courier New]PiPPlayer.ini[/font], and the [font=Courier New]PiPPlayer[/font] folder from [font=Courier New]Data/SKSE/Plugins[/font]. Safe at any time.

